{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '652,685p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n 'slow-test\\\\?|DATOM_SLOW' test/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc test/dao/test_slow.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest' test/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"\nActivating mise before the `cd` and `mise trust` leaves the repo-selected tools\n(flutter in particular) off PATH: the Dart lane then dies in seconds with \"Can't\nfind flutter on PATH\", and so does `bb build:yin-repl-peer`.\n\n### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n\n\"One lane set at a time\" and \"one Dart lane at a time\" are per-machine rules about\nCPU: they exist because a laptop has 8 cores. They are not a rule about repos.\n`test.subsystems.md` section 5 item 6 says the same (\"on one machine where\navoidable\"). The laptop additionally never runs the slow tier or the nightly\ndriver (see the sharded-lane section) — a full slow tier there reached a load\naverage over 100 on 2026-11-01; the remote hosts own that tier. On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\nlanes may overlap, with these limits:\n\n- **JVM and Dart lanes must not share one clone.** `src/dev/affected.clj`\n  (`serialized-pairs`, the `[:clj :cljd]` pair) serializes them whenever a JVM test\n  runs the cljd compiler, and some do (`yin.repl.build-test`,\n  `yin.vm.linker.cross-host-transfer-test`, `dao.stream.ws-project-cross-jvm-test`);\n  the compiler writes the clone's `lib/cljd-out` and `build/`. A second scratch clone\n  gives the Dart lane its own copies, so the two lanes then overlap safely. This is\n  by the design's own reasoning (\"each worktree owns its own `cljd-out`\"), not yet\n  verified by a measured run.\n- **JVM and Node may share a clone.** Node writes `target/` and `.shadow-cljs/`; the\n  JVM lane only reads `target/yin-repl.js`.\n- **One Dart lane per host at a time**, even across clones: the lane shards up to\n  `min(8, cores)` Flutter processes and shares the host's Flutter cache.\n- **Different branches in different clones** are independent, so two branches may\n  run on one host if its cores and RAM allow (62 GB each).\n- Do not treat this as permission to overlap lanes on the laptop.\n\nThe first run on shiva (2026-10-11) overlapped JVM and Dart in one clone before\nthis rule was written down; its results are advisory until repeated with a\nseparate Dart clone.\ntest/dao/test_slow.cljc:6:   runs only when DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1, otherwise it prints a skip notice.\"\ntest/dao/test_slow.cljc:10:(def env-name \"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\")\ntest/dao/test_slow.cljc:28:    (println \"SKIP slow test\" test-name \"(set DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 to run)\")))\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:50:(deftest a-toy-frontend-evaluates-on-every-vm-test\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:65:(deftest the-standard-languages-select-by-id-test\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:81:(deftest a-newer-revision-leaves-a-live-session-unchanged-test\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:98:(deftest an-unavailable-frontend-answers-without-fallback-test\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:121:(deftest the-antlr-id-is-installed-on-every-host-test\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:128:(deftest a-core-session-with-no-catalog-has-no-frontend-test\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:134:(deftest a-revision-is-pinned-by-id-and-revision-test\ntest/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:155:(deftest an-explicit-parser-service-makes-an-id-available-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:81:(deftest descriptor-validation-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:149:(deftest immutable-projection-export-presence-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:160:(deftest capabilities-refuse-before-emission-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:214:(deftest persistent-profile-e2e-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:225:(deftest policy-traps-and-guest-cleanup-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:265:(deftest cross-carrier-keys-and-binding-presence-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:290:(deftest clojure-python-clojure-unwind-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:345:(deftest entry-preserves-verbatim-values-and-shared-gensym-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:358:(deftest default-selection-and-snapshot-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:379:(deftest default-repl-reports-guest-errors-and-keeps-the-session-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:397:(deftest profile-program-root-goldens-test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
