{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"head -45 test/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc; rg -n 'deftest.*store|deftest' test/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc | tail -18; rg -n 'deftest.*store' test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.serve-test\n  \"The server side of the DaoStream Yin REPL, over the request-and-response\n   service of docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md section 5.\n\n   The host is the in-process loopback net (yin.repl.net-fixture): its\n   `:bind!` and `:unbind!` deposit lifecycle data, and a real\n   `yin.repl.connect` client attaches through its `:connect!`, so the\n   endpoint's sessions, drain and stop are observed from a client on every\n   host.  Nothing here binds a port.  The requests/answers interpreter is\n   tested at the level serve.cljc itself owns -- the shared buffers\n   `serve!` composes -- since the wire and the mirror answering it are\n   dao.stream.remote-channel's own, already proven by its test suite; the\n   demo REPL flow over a real socket is proven end to end in\n   yin.repl.serve-connect-wire-test (JVM).\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n            [yin.repl.driver :as driver]\n            [yin.repl.main :as main]\n            [yin.repl.net-fixture :as fixture]\n            [yin.repl.serve :as serve]\n            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; An injected host listener\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- endpoint!\n  ([] (endpoint! {}))\n  ([extra]\n   (let [h (fixture/host)]\n     {:host h\n      :endpoint (serve/serve! (merge {:bind-port 8080\n                                      :host (:adapter h)}\n                                     extra))})))\n\n\n(defn- texts\n190:(deftest stopping-after-bind-threw-never-calls-unbind-or-waits\n208:(deftest a-synchronous-unbind-failure-resolves-stop-locally\n225:(deftest stop-ends-the-served-media-before-it-closes-the-session\n256:(deftest attachment-departure-is-noticed\n270:(deftest a-serving-gap-is-counted-and-serving-continues\n307:(deftest a-request-evaluates-against-the-shared-shell-and-answers-once\n318:(deftest store-switching-stays-on-the-local-driver\n353:(deftest failed-driver-installation-releases-the-replacement-only\n373:(deftest a-late-store-refusal-restores-memory-for-the-driver-and-endpoint\n394:(deftest the-shared-shell-is-threaded-serially-across-requests\n408:(deftest a-served-host-function-renders-as-the-local-marker\n432:(deftest an-unknown-operation-is-a-portable-error-not-a-thrown-handler\n446:(deftest incomplete-input-is-answered-and-never-crosses-a-callers-boundary\n467:(deftest a-malformed-but-correlatable-request-is-answered-not-silently-dropped\n480:(deftest a-well-formed-request-with-an-unsafe-id-is-dropped-not-evaluated\n497:(deftest an-uncorrelatable-value-is-dropped-as-a-diagnostic\n509:(deftest the-summary-is-plain-data\n525:(deftest the-composition-registers-the-v4-format-record\n320:(deftest the-store-command-parses-and-checks-the-composition-options\n381:(deftest a-dht-store-with-no-peers-is-solo-and-opens-no-socket\n993:(deftest a-plain-join-and-the-repl-store-exclude-each-other\n1138:(deftest a-solo-store-swaps-in-and-releases-its-lock-on-departure\n1245:(deftest a-failed-composition-swap-leaves-the-old-store-locked-and-writable\n1938:(deftest a-dht-store-refuses-a-second-content-source\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
